"Maya [ps|lives] in a small but welcoming flat with her mother and younger brother. She usually [ps|gets up] at seven, [ps|makes] her bed and [ps|opens] the windows before breakfast. Her mother [ps|believes] that a tidy home [ps|creates] a calm mind, so everyone [ps|has] a few household responsibilities. Maya [ps|does] the laundry twice a week, while her brother [ps|takes out] the rubbish and [ps|waters] the plants.",
"Today, however, the family [pc|is preparing] for a special Sunday lunch. Maya [pc|is dusting] the shelves, her brother [pc|is setting] the table, and their mother [pc|is cooking] in the kitchen. Maya [pc|is trying] to finish everything before their aunt [ps|arrives]. She [ppc|has been cleaning] since nine o'clock, and she [pp|has already polished] the old wooden cabinet in the living room.",
"The cabinet [ps|is] Maya's favourite possession. It [pas|belonged] to her grandmother, who [pas|bought] it many years ago. When Maya [pas|was] a child, she [pas|used to hide] little notes inside its drawers. Last year, while she [pac|was sorting] through the cabinet, she [pas|found] a tiny silver key wrapped in a piece of cloth. She [pap|had never seen] it before, and she [pas|wondered] what it opened.",
"By the time her grandmother [pas|visited] that afternoon, Maya [pap|had searched] every drawer but [pap|had not discovered] the key's purpose. Her grandmother [pas|smiled] and [pas|explained] that she [pap|had kept] an old jewellery box in the attic. She also said that she [papc|had been looking] for the key for years, because she [pap|had forgotten] where she put it. Maya [pac|was listening] carefully when her grandmother suddenly [pas|remembered] the box's location.",
"A few minutes later, they [pas|went] upstairs. Maya's grandmother [pas|opened] a dusty trunk, and there it was: a small blue jewellery box. The key [pas|fitted] perfectly. Inside, they [pas|found] a delicate bracelet, two faded photographs and a handwritten recipe. Maya [pp|has kept] the bracelet safe ever since. She [pp|has shown] it to only a few people, because it [ps|means] a great deal to her.",
"Now, whenever Maya [ps|looks] at the bracelet, she [ps|remembers] her grandmother's patience and kindness. She [pp|has learned] that possessions are not valuable simply because they are expensive; they can carry stories and memories. Her family [ppc|has been sharing] these memories more often lately, and Maya [pc|is thinking] of writing them down in a family notebook.",
"Last Sunday, while the family [pac|were having] lunch, Maya [pas|told] everyone about her idea. Her brother [pas|laughed] because he [papc|had been avoiding] housework all morning, but he [pas|promised] to help. Before that day, he [pap|had never volunteered] to organise anything. Since then, he [pp|has become] more responsible: he [ps|does] his chores without being reminded, and yesterday he [pac|was even cleaning] the kitchen when Maya [pas|came] home.",
